{"id":"u-fd7d5a35-c757-48ef-a7a5-798fb4d430f4","src":"community","title":"Hornet","author":"Adithya N.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/IeVoWG-ul-split-hornet","desc":"Selectively chooses dynamic double progression or double progression for certain exercises. Does not make sense to apply the same progression strategy to all exercises.  Staggers Push and Pull exercises on Upper Days.  \n\nRest Times:\n\nLower, Bench, Incline Bench, Pullups, Shoulder Press : 2 Minutes 30 seconds\nEverything Else: 2 Minutes\n\n\nProgression Strategy:\n\nFor any exercise where you can go to failure safely, and not worry too much about form, work in the 4-8 rep range and add weight based on the first set. Some exercises include Dumbell Curls, Tricep Extensions, Lat Pulldown, Pullups, etc. Anything done on a machine that doesnt have something that falls on top of you at the end, or leaves you with a disgusting pump even when your form wavers a little bit. \n\nIf you want to keep your form clean and minimize risky failure, work in the 6 - 10 rep range, and add weight when both sets have hit the top range. Some exercises that might be worth considering in this rep range could be the Barbell Bench, Lateral Raises, Deadlifts etc. \n\nProgression Samples:\nRep Range - 4 - 8 - 1st Set Based Progression\n40*7, 40*6 => 40*8, 40*6 => 45*4 , 40*7 => 45*4, 40*8  => 45*5, 45*4  \nIf your first set is right at the bottom of the prescribed rep range, the second set has to be reduced in weight compared to the first.\nIf your second set is right at the top of the prescribed rep range,  next time around your second set weight has to go up. \nDo not try to beat the rep range. Stop if you can hit the weight for the prescribed set of reps. increase the weight next workout.","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-04-25T04:31:53.125Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper","Arms","Upper","Lower"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Wide Grip)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Neutral Grip, Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"V-Handle Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Preacher Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Reverse Pec Deck","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Overhead Extension (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Reverse Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"V-Handle Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Wide Grip)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Neutral Grip, Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"V-Handle Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Preacher Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Shrug (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Wide Grip)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Neutral Grip, Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Rais